From ce721460a50c745c53f51afa25e510a0d1139310 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 01:24:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] usb: storage: ignore UAS for the HIKSEMI portable SSD
 (2bdf:0300)

With this bridge driven by uas, the device stops answering when more
than a handful of commands are queued: 30 s later the SCSI layer
aborts every command in flight (uas_eh_abort_handler) and the device is
reset. It happens at every start of Kodi from such a drive, a few
seconds after Kodi begins to read and write in parallel: seen in every
session recorded on two machines with different xHCI controllers (an
AMD laptop, with 18 to 30 reads in flight; an AM5 desktop, with 10 to
18 writes), since the drive was first used. What the user sees is the
system standing still for half a minute.

The kernel already has an entry of this kind for another Hiksemi
enclosure (090c:2000). With US_FL_IGNORE_UAS the drive is handled by
usb-storage, one command at a time.

Not tested with the drive: the entry is the one the kernel uses for
bridges that fail this way, and the drive is the one it was seen on.
---
 drivers/usb/storage/unusual_uas.h | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/storage/unusual_uas.h b/drivers/usb/storage/unusual_uas.h
index d6f86d5..e66542f 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/storage/unusual_uas.h
+++ b/drivers/usb/storage/unusual_uas.h
@@ -174,6 +174,19 @@ UNUSUAL_DEV(0x2537, 0x1068, 0x0000, 0x9999,
 		USB_SC_DEVICE, USB_PR_DEVICE, NULL,
 		US_FL_IGNORE_UAS),
 
+/*
+ * HIKSEMI portable SSD: with more than a handful of commands queued the
+ * bridge stops answering (uas_eh_abort_handler on every command in
+ * flight 30 s later, then a reset of the device). Seen at every start
+ * of a media player from it, on two machines with different host
+ * controllers, with reads and with writes.
+ */
+UNUSUAL_DEV(0x2bdf, 0x0300, 0x0000, 0x9999,
+		"HIKSEMI",
+		"Portable SSD",
+		USB_SC_DEVICE, USB_PR_DEVICE, NULL,
+		US_FL_IGNORE_UAS),
+
 /*
